  "geometryBasis": "Drawn against the named 27-node building outline with the same Wikidata identification as its separately mapped historic parcel. The source terrain and west entrance nearest Weimin Street fix the horizontal and vertical frame.",
  "sectionBasis": "The owner records two storeys, arcades on four sides, three octagonal projections, and multiple generations of gable. The heritage ministry records the west-facing brick mansion. The 1908 original album view establishes the original arcade and cornice vocabulary.",
  "limitations": [
    "The present restored mansion has the lower triangular third-generation pediment. The original high rounded clock-shaped gable is recorded as historic and is not installed on the contemporary roof.",
    "Native walls and major projections are fixed within the 27-point outline. Opening sequence, cornice profiles, tile color and wall heights are estimated from the 1908 evidence and written current heritage details.",
    "Only the Western residence and its front steps are represented. The vanished Japanese timber counterpart, garden contents, and separately mapped air-raid shelter are excluded."
